rveillance of DBMD in four states\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Denominators used for rate calculations were the male resident population from the U.S. Census Bureau's 2007 population estimates\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Because of the progressive nature of DBMD, wheelchair use was assumed to continue after initiation.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Cases lost to follow-up were excluded from analyses because neither residency nor survival could be confirmed.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"[(No. - lost to follow-up - deaths) / (No. - lost to follow-up)] x 100.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\"]}", "type": "text"}]}